      "name": "Write Rows",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.4,
      "position": [
        3136,
        -16
      ],
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "credentials": {
        "airtableTokenApi": {
          "id": "RZ2SX89iUyF4aEWJ",
          "name": "Airtable"
        }
      },
      "notes": "The one row writer (replaced the Update Record Airtable node 2026-09-02, the same defect that killed Waterfall Emails executions 9812 and 9813): PATCH /v0/{base}/{table} with {records (ten per request), typecast: true}, 200 ms apart, so 50 rows per second against the Airtable node's measured 4.5. No retry: a 429 locks the base for 30 s; a request that is not 2xx counts every row in it as a write error, names its record ids, and the pass carries on to the log."
    },
